1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:03,450
We've always known that
tokenisation is the future.

2
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:06,250
Real-world asset tokenisation
has been a very hot topic.

3
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:08,300
It's been something a lot of people want to do.

4
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:10,250
But the question has always been:
how do we do this?

5
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:10,700
Yeah.

6
00:00:10,730 --> 00:00:14,570
And that's very much why Tokeniser exists.

7
00:00:14,570 --> 00:00:17,290
It's meant to be that gateway,
that ability for those issuers.

8
00:00:17,290 --> 00:00:21,290
And as we've seen with our experience
with companies, and soon to be in

9
00:00:21,290 --> 00:00:23,800
working with funds and trustees
on the same matter,

10
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:27,330
we want to give them a platform
that's familiar, easy to use,

11
00:00:27,330 --> 00:00:31,300
that very much traditional,
in this sense, Web 2.0 style interface,

12
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:35,810
but at the same time is
powered by and enables them

13
00:00:35,810 --> 00:00:38,290
to essentially tokenise their assets.

14
00:00:38,290 --> 00:00:42,530
So it makes it easy for the issuers
to essentially get onto

15
00:00:42,530 --> 00:00:44,250
the Redbelly Network.

16
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:48,570
It makes it easy for their shareholders,
note holders, unit holders,

17
00:00:48,570 --> 00:00:51,650
whoever has invested in these issuers,
to get onto the Redbelly Network.

18
00:00:51,650 --> 00:00:54,650
It makes it easy for those tokens
that have been minted

19
00:00:54,650 --> 00:00:56,250
and issued via the Tokeniser platform

20
00:00:56,250 --> 00:00:58,400
to be transacted on the Redbelly Network.
